          "title_zh": "为终端智能体学习可泛化行为",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.22631v3",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2608.22631",
          "summary": "The paper proposes the Agentic Compositional Generalization hypothesis, that RL mainly shapes high-level decision-making which composes and routes skills acquired during pretraining and SFT, and introduces River, a recipe that filters low-quality environments and augments outcome rewards with process-level behavior regularization. River reaches the best performance among evaluated open-source RL-trained 8B models on four terminal-agent benchmarks and improves RL gains by 106% and 30% using fewer than 30% of the TMax training environments.",
