          "title_zh": "GeoRisk-RAG：通过选择性回答提升 RAG 可靠性的层次感知风险框架",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.22634v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2608.22634",
          "summary": "GeoRisk-RAG estimates geographic applicability before generating a response, using a DAG-based distance over geographic hierarchies to decide when to answer selectively in natural-hazard domains. On a held-out wildfire QA dataset it reduces false-confidence rates to 0.009 versus about 0.090 for semantic-similarity and reranking baselines, while achieving higher human preference alignment.",
