          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2608.22636",
          "summary": "The paper develops a stable infinite-dimensional linear function approximation framework for Q-learning from a single Markovian behavior-policy trajectory, using reconstruction and compression operators whose nonexpansiveness yields a contractive latent Bellman map with a unique fixed point. It proposes two stochastic approximation algorithms with sup-norm convergence bounds whose leading term is of order O(n^{-1/2}), controlled through covering numbers of the latent space rather than its dimension.",
